--- body ---
## Context

Precondition ticket, not a fourth ladder gap. Filed against tracker 0613
(goal 1 of the ladder, zoteus target), whose child 0630 (drafting
`UNINSTALL.md` as the R15 removal procedure) re-measured and flagged this
exact gap as an open precondition on 2026-09-03: `R15-uninstall-removes-declared-state`
cannot be graded green for zoteus until the arena redirects `TMPDIR` and the
`XDG_*` roots, per the 2026-09-03 ruling recorded in 0613's own log
(2026-09-03T12:14Z entry: "the arena must redirect TMPDIR and the XDG roots
before the clause can be graded at all").

This is framed as a **precondition**, not a lettered gap, because it is not
itself one of the three requirement clauses (R10, R15, R22) the tracker's
matrix grades — it is a measurement-integrity condition the R15 uninstall
clause depends on, the same way the dedicated-account precondition (ticket
0625) was. 0613's own tracker table lists three gaps (A/B/C); this closes
neither A nor C and is not inserted as a fourth row for the same reason 0625
was not.

**The mechanical defect, independent of zoteus's specific footprint.**
`bench/acceptance/assertions.py`'s `Snapshot.of(root)` (`os.walk(root)`) only
ever looks under the harness-owned arena. `check_residue_inventory` diffs two
snapshots of `arena`. A write outside `arena` — under an unredirected `HOME`
or `TMPDIR` — is not merely uncounted, it is structurally unreachable by the
sweep: confirmed by placing a marker file directly under a substitute
operator-home and showing `Snapshot.of(arena)` reports zero new files before
and after, even though the marker exists (see Verification, mechanism-level
control).

Before this ticket, `bench/acceptance/adapters/zoteus.py`'s `_env()` declared
only `ZOTEUS_*` variables and `running()` merged them onto the *full*
operator `os.environ` unchanged (`{**os.environ, **env}`) — the one adapter
of the acceptance layer's five that redirected nothing, not even `HOME`.
Four siblings (`beaver.py`, `zotero_core_6012.py`, `zotero_mcp.py`,
`zotseek.py`) already redirect `HOME` into `arena / "home"`; none of the five
redirected `TMPDIR`; only `zotero_mcp.py` touched any `XDG_*` var
(`XDG_CACHE_HOME`, blanked).

## Footprint investigated (not assumed) — SHA `b0e0bc8` (v1.13.0, `UPSTREAM`'s
pinned reviewed SHA; `fork/` was rebuilt clean at this SHA for this ticket,
`npm ci && npm run build`, both succeeded)

1. **`HOME` has a real, if narrow, source hit — not just the sibling
   convention.** `fork/src/lib/paths.ts`:
   - `defaultDataDir()` falls back to `env.XDG_DATA_HOME ?? homedir()+'/.local/share'`
     only when `ZOTEUS_DATA_DIR` is unset — never true for this adapter,
     since `_env()` always sets it and it is checked first in
     `config.ts:401`. Not load-bearing today, but the same shape as 0630's
     earlier finding about `XDG_DATA_HOME`, so blanked for consistency.
   - `defaultZoteroDataDir()` falls back to `homedir() + '/Zotero'` whenever
     `ZOTERO_DATA_DIR` is unset — and the adapter's own `_env()` only sets
     `ZOTERO_DATA_DIR` when `self.zotero_data_dir` was supplied to the
     constructor (an optional argument, default `""`; see
     `zoteus.py`'s `_env()`, `if self.zotero_data_dir: env["ZOTERO_DATA_DIR"] = ...`).
     **This is the load-bearing hit**: any run that does not pass
     `zotero_data_dir` — e.g. a cloud-API-only configuration, per this
     project's own `project_live_smoke_recipe` memory ("no desktop Zotero →
     force cloud transport") — resolves this path against whatever `HOME`
     the process was given. Unredirected, that is the operator's real home
     directory's `Zotero` folder, entirely outside the arena.
2. **`TMPDIR` has zero source hits**, in `fork/src/` and in the six actual
   runtime npm dependencies (`@modelcontextprotocol/sdk`, `citeproc`,
   `cors`, `express`, `express-rate-limit`, `zod` — grepped `package.json`;
   `@huggingface/transformers` is confirmed **not** a direct dependency,
   `grep -n transformers fork/package.json` returns nothing). Grepped the
   built dependency tree for `os.tmpdir` and found it only in
   **devDependencies** (`prettier`, `@types/node`), which never run in the
   spawned server process. Redirected **defensively**: no source hit to
   cite, warranted because (a) Node/npm and any native addon a dependency
   pulls in commonly consult it, and (b) a standalone
   `@huggingface/transformers` install reached through
   `ZOTEUS_TRANSFORMERS_PATH` (per the live-smoke-recipe memory, installed
   at `~/.zoteus-deps/node_modules`, never inside `fork/node_modules`) is a
   real code path this adapter drives in real runs, and its native
   `onnxruntime` addon's temp-file behaviour is unaudited from this repo's
   side. The model cache itself is not the concern — `env.cacheDir` is
   already pinned under `<ZOTEUS_DATA_DIR>/models` (ticket 0630's finding,
   confirmed still true at this SHA) — what is unaudited is everything else
   such a runtime, or npm/Node itself, might touch.
3. **`XDG_CACHE_HOME`/`XDG_CONFIG_HOME`/`XDG_STATE_HOME` have zero source
   hits** in `fork/src/`. Blanked for consistency with `zotero_mcp.py`'s
   treatment of `XDG_CACHE_HOME` and because `_env()`'s dict is merged over
   `os.environ` with **no delete** (`mcp_drive.Server`/`running()` both do
   `{**os.environ, **env}`) — an *absent* key passes the operator's real
   ambient value through unchanged; only a blank key closes it.
4. **Actually spawned the real built server** (behavioral control, not just
   source reading) with a substitute-operator `HOME`/`TMPDIR` (never the
   real ones) and both the unpatched and patched `_env()`: in this target's
   default configuration (no `zotero_data_dir` supplied, so the real
   `defaultZoteroDataDir()` fallback above is reached but only *read*, never
   written to), **nothing landed under either substitute directory in
   either arm** — see Verification. This is the finding ticket 0630
   anticipated ("if literally nothing lands there for zoteus specifically —
   that itself is a finding to record precisely"): zoteus's actual runtime
   footprint outside its declared data directory is empty, measured, not
   assumed. The fix still closes the mechanical gap (item 1's `HOME` hit is
   real, even though it manifests as an out-of-arena *read* rather than a
   *write* in the configuration tested) and matches the other four
   adapters' standing convention.

## Relevant files

- `bench/acceptance/adapters/zoteus.py` — `__init__` (added `self.home`,
  `self.tmp`), `_env()` (added `HOME`, `TMPDIR`, four blanked `XDG_*` keys),
  `running()` (added the two `mkdir`s). Diff is additive; no existing key
  changed.
- `tests/test_acceptance_adapter_zoteus.py` — four new offline tests exercise
  `_env()` directly (no process spawned): redirection, XDG blanking,
  regression guard on the pre-existing keys, and a positive control that
  reproduces `running()`'s own merge (`{**os.environ, **env}`) against a
  deliberately different ambient value and asserts the declared dict wins.
- `bench/acceptance/assertions.py` — read only, not modified:
  `Snapshot.of`/`check_residue_inventory` (~lines 108-172, 394-457), cited
  above for the mechanism.

## Actions

1. Add `self.home`/`self.tmp` to `Zoteus.__init__`, `HOME`/`TMPDIR`/four
   blanked `XDG_*` keys to `_env()`, and the two `mkdir`s to `running()`.
   Additive only — `ZOTEUS_DATA_DIR` and every other existing key untouched.
2. Add offline tests to `tests/test_acceptance_adapter_zoteus.py` mirroring
   `test_acceptance_adapter_zotero_mcp.py`'s
   `test_the_environment_blanks_every_variable_the_target_reads`.
3. Prove red-before-green: run the new tests against the unpatched `_env()`
   (a git-blob copy of the pre-fix file) and confirm the redirection/blanking/
   override-precedence tests fail red; confirm they pass green against the
   fix.
4. Actually spawn the built server (behavioral control) with a substitute
   operator `HOME`/`TMPDIR`, unpatched vs. patched, and record what lands
   where.
5. Mechanism-level control: show `Snapshot.of(arena)` cannot see a marker
   file placed outside `arena`, independent of zoteus's specific footprint.
6. Generalization check: run `check_residue_inventory` against the patched
   adapter with the *outer* ambient `$HOME` pre-populated with realistic
   clutter (dotfiles, fake `.cache/`, fake `.npm/`, a fake `Zotero/zotero.sqlite`)
   and confirm the sweep still reports `pass`/0 residue, and the clutter is
   untouched — proof the redirected `HOME` **replaces** the ambient value
   rather than merging into it.

## Test

`tests/test_acceptance_adapter_zoteus.py`, four new tests (offline, no
process spawned, mirrors the zotero_mcp adapter's own environment test):
- `test_the_environment_redirects_home_and_tmpdir_into_the_arena`
- `test_the_environment_blanks_the_xdg_roots`
- `test_the_environment_leaves_the_existing_keys_unchanged` (regression
  guard: additive-only constraint)
- `test_the_declared_environment_overrides_an_ambient_override` (positive
  control: reproduces `running()`'s merge against a deliberately different
  ambient value)

## Verification

- [x] `_env()` sets `HOME`/`TMPDIR` inside the arena and blanks the four
      `XDG_*` roots; `ZOTEUS_DATA_DIR` and every other existing key
      unchanged (diffed against `git show HEAD:...` before this ticket)
- [x] Red control: the four new tests run against a git-blob copy of the
      unpatched `_env()` — 3 of 4 fail red (`test_the_environment_redirects_home_and_tmpdir_into_the_arena`:
      `KeyError: 'HOME'`; `test_the_environment_blanks_the_xdg_roots`:
      `XDG_CACHE_HOME` absent, not blanked; `test_the_declared_environment_overrides_an_ambient_override`:
      ambient value survives the merge). Only the additive-keys-unchanged
      test passes unpatched, correctly — it asserts nothing about the new
      keys.
- [x] Green control: all 5 tests in the file (the 4 new + the pre-existing
      posture test) pass against the fix.
- [x] Behavioral control: the real built server (SHA `b0e0bc8`) actually
      spawned with a substitute-operator `HOME`/`TMPDIR` (never the real
      ones), unpatched vs. patched — in this target's default configuration
      (no `zotero_data_dir` supplied), nothing landed under either
      substitute directory in either arm. Recorded as a measured finding
      about zoteus's narrow footprint, not assumed; the mechanical gap (a
      write, had one occurred, would have been invisible to the sweep) is
      still closed by the fix and matches the sibling convention.
- [x] Mechanism-level control: a marker file placed directly under a
      substitute operator-home is invisible to `Snapshot.of(arena)` before
      and after — `created` comes back empty even though the marker exists.
      Demonstrates the invisibility claim independent of what zoteus
      specifically writes.
- [x] Generalization check: `check_residue_inventory` run against the
      patched adapter with a realistically cluttered outer ambient `$HOME`
      (dotfiles, fake `.cache/`, fake `.npm/_cacache/`, a fake
      `Zotero/zotero.sqlite`) — `result: pass`, `residue_count: 0`,
      `created_count: 0`, and the clutter file's content unchanged
      afterward, confirming the redirect replaces rather than merges.
- [x] `python3 -m pytest tests/test_acceptance_adapter_zoteus.py -v` — 5
      passed. Full suite `python3 -m pytest tests/ -q` — 824 passed, 14
      skipped, 2 pre-existing unrelated failures
      (`tests/test_summarize_0120.py`, `FileNotFoundError: sqlite3` — the
      `sqlite3` CLI binary is absent from this machine's `PATH`, unrelated
      to this change; confirmed with `which sqlite3` exiting 1).
- [x] `ruff check --select E4,E7,E9,F bench/acceptance/adapters/zoteus.py
      tests/test_acceptance_adapter_zoteus.py` — all checks passed.

## Invariants

- `ZOTEUS_DATA_DIR` and every pre-existing `_env()` key unchanged — this is
  additive to `_env()`, not a restructuring, per the task brief's explicit
  constraint (other parallel work in this repo reads this file).
- No non-default target option introduced; `HOME`/`TMPDIR`/`XDG_*` are
  process-level sandboxing, the same category the four sibling adapters
  already treat this way, never a flag passed to the target.
- 0613's tracker is not closed by this ticket (gap C, R22, remains open and
  is out of scope); referenced with `Ticket-ref:`, not closed.

## Exit criteria

- [x] `bench/acceptance/adapters/zoteus.py` redirects `HOME`/`TMPDIR` into
      arena-scoped directories and blanks the four `XDG_*` roots, additive
      to the existing `_env()`.
- [x] Footprint investigated against a freshly built reviewed-SHA checkout,
      not copied from the sibling adapters or assumed; each redirected var
      states whether it has a direct source hit or is defensive, and why.
- [x] Red-before-green demonstrated on the unit tests, plus an actual
      spawn of the real server as a behavioral control, plus a
      mechanism-level control independent of zoteus's specific footprint,
      plus the generalization check with a populated outer `$HOME`.
- [x] 0613's own log records this finding closed (append-only; the
      TMPDIR/XDG precondition entries from 2026-09-03 stand as history).
